From: Richard Parsons <tuxbox.guru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 20:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] logging: fall back to fmtlib when libstdc++ has no <format>

std::format only reached libstdc++ in GCC 13.  PetaLinux 2023.2 is Yocto
langdale, whose cross toolchain is GCC 12.2 and ships no <format> header
at all, so the whole tree fails to compile at the first include.

<format> is used in exactly one place -- the deferred formatting in
decnet/common/logging.h -- and fmtlib is the library std::format was
standardised from, with the same format(), the same format_string<> and
the same "{}" grammar, so the fallback is a namespace swap.  Selected
automatically on __cpp_lib_format, which keeps a GCC 13+ host build on
std::format and needing no fmtlib at all; -DDN_USE_FMTLIB forces it.

Verified both ways against fmt 9.1.0 (the version meta-oe carries):
release build clean with no new warnings, and samples/endnode.conf comes
up with byte-identical log lines.

Upstream-Status: Pending [sent to github.com/RichardPar/cppdecnet]

diff --git a/include/decnet/common/logging.h b/include/decnet/common/logging.h
index 9b6dbd9..5802774 100644
--- a/include/decnet/common/logging.h
+++ b/include/decnet/common/logging.h
@@ -8,9 +8,25 @@
 #ifndef DECNET_COMMON_LOGGING_H
 #define DECNET_COMMON_LOGGING_H
 
-#include <format>
+// PORT: std::format only reached libstdc++ in GCC 13.  PetaLinux 2023.2
+// (Yocto langdale) cross-compiles with GCC 12.2, whose libstdc++ has no
+// <format> at all, so fall back to fmtlib -- the library std::format was
+// standardised from, with the same format(), the same format_string<> and
+// the same "{}" grammar.  Define DN_USE_FMTLIB to force the fallback on a
+// toolchain that does have <format>.
+#include <version>
+
+#if defined(DN_USE_FMTLIB) || !defined(__cpp_lib_format)
+#  include <fmt/format.h>
+#  define DN_FORMAT_NS ::fmt
+#else
+#  include <format>
+#  define DN_FORMAT_NS ::std
+#endif
+
 #include <string>
 #include <string_view>
+#include <utility>
 
 namespace decnet::logging {
 
@@ -39,11 +55,13 @@ void set_thread_name (std::string name);
 // The one function that actually writes; the macros below format first.
 void emit (Level l, std::string_view msg) noexcept;
 
+// The parameter is named `f` rather than `fmt` so that it cannot shadow the
+// fmt namespace in the fallback build.
 template <typename... A>
-void log (Level l, std::format_string<A...> fmt, A &&...args)
+void log (Level l, DN_FORMAT_NS::format_string<A...> f, A &&...args)
 {
     if (enabled (l))
-        emit (l, std::format (fmt, std::forward<A> (args)...));
+        emit (l, DN_FORMAT_NS::format (f, std::forward<A> (args)...));
 }
 
 }   // namespace decnet::logging
